
This repository contains scripts used in extracting metrics from STR images generated by REViewer tool (https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-022-01085-z).

EXTRACT INFORMATION FROM IMAGES

The scripts:
(1) get_reviewer_image_sections_new.py : This script gets the information field from the input image file {locus}.svg.
  usage:
  python3 get_reviewer_image_sections_new.py {VariantId}.svg {VariantId}_output1 {VariantId}_output2

  The command above will generate the two output files (file names provided as input in command):
  {VariantId}_output1 has information used in machine learning (ML) training.
  {VariantId}_output2 is instead not ivolved in ML method. It contains information about the image coordinate
      * where the first read of upper haplotype  starts
      * where the read of bottom haplotype  starts
      * where the repeat region in the upper haplotype starts
      * where the repeat region in the bottom haplotype starts


(2) count_nucleotides_from_reads_Total_v3.sh and ount_nucleotides_from_reads_ORANGE_v3.sh
The scripts get the total counts of nucleotide interruptions within the reads aligned to a reference sequence in the image.
The input files are the image file {VariantId}.svg and {VariantId}_output2 (the file generated from previous step)
usage:
bash count_nucleotides_from_reads_Total_v3.sh {VariantId}.svg {VariantId}_output2 > {VariantId}_TotalCounts
bash count_nucleotides_from_reads_ORANGE_v3.sh {VariantId}.svg {VariantId}_output2 > {VariantId}_orangeCounts
count_nucleotides_from_reads_Total_v3.sh : This gets the total counts of interrupting nucleotides in entire size of aligned read shown in the image.
count_nucleotides_from_reads_ORANGE_v3.sh : This gets the total counts of interrupting nucleotides in repeat region (orange coloured region) of aligned reads in the image.

(3) combine_files.py : This combines everything into a file named {VariantId}_AllMetrices
usage:
python3 combine_files.py {VariantId}.metrics.tsv {VariantId}_output1 {locus}_TotalCounts {VariantId}_orangeCounts {VariantId}_AllMetrices
Here one of the the input file  {VariantId}.metrics.tsv is generated from REViewer tool.

(4) merge_csv_files.py : Final step is to combine all {VariantId}_AllMetrices files genrated from each loci of a given sample into a single txt file.
 This script will also remove the images with NA values automatically and collect the failed images into a separate metrics file named
 image_list : List of {VariantId}_AllMetrices to combine in a single file.

 usage:
 python merge_csv_files.py -i image_list -p $sampleId

--------

COLLECT XGBTREE SCORES

This requires R 4.1.0 to be installed.
It also requires EH output produced from TERRA workflow (https://github.com/broadinstitute/gatk-sv/blob/str_v1.2/wdl/ExpansionHunterScatter.wdl) in tsv format.
Example file is "HG00514.1_json_files.variants_reduced.tsv"
(5) Collect_xgbtree_scores.R : The R scripts will compute xgbTree scores using trained xgbTree model.

usage:
Rscript Collect_xgbtree_scores.R HG00514.1_json_files.variants_reduced.tsv $sampleId"_metrics.csv" $sampleId
